# The unquantised ONNX export is tracked with Git LFS so CI can restore it
# and assert the AI inference path actually executed — see
# docs/adr/0004-ci-gates-detection-the-ai-is-smoke-tested.md.
#
# This used to be the quantised export (32MB) instead. Switched 2026-08-15:
# static INT8 quantisation of the resnet50_multiscale backbone (added
# 2026-08-14) turned out to need real, dedicated debugging effort --
# argmax agreement against the unquantised model topped out at 63% across
# five independently-fixed bugs (wrong quant format, missing
# pre-processing, unstandardised calibration inputs, per-tensor instead of
# per-channel weights, MinMax instead of Percentile calibration -- see the
# ai_export.py commit history around that date), with errors persistently
# collapsing toward one class regardless of which knob changed. Shipping
# that would mean the "AI path executed" smoke test no longer implies "and
# produced a sane answer" -- worse than the gap it exists to close.
#
# Trade-off accepted for now: this costs real Git LFS bandwidth headroom.
# The other artefacts in models/ stay gitignored, too large to version:
#
#   visual_ai.onnx           1MB   <- tracked here (graph)
#   visual_ai.onnx.data    159MB   <- tracked here (weights)
#   visual_ai.pt            160MB
#   visual_ai.quant.onnx     88MB  (not correctness-verified, not tracked)
#   visual_ai.ckpt.pt        410MB
#
# Git LFS free tier is 1GB/month, so this leaves roughly 6 CI restores/month
# (down from ~31 with the quantised file). If that's too tight for this
# project's actual push volume, the smoke job should move to a schedule
# rather than running on every push -- the detection gate above does not
# depend on the model either way. Revert to quantised once someone finds
# the sixth bug (errors collapsing to one class across five different
# quantisation configurations points at something architecture-specific
# still unfound, not a calibration-tuning problem).
.visual-regression/models/visual_ai.onnx filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
.visual-regression/models/visual_ai.onnx.data filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# Normalise line endings so a file committed from Windows and one from a Linux
# runner do not differ by \r alone. Without this the repo already emits a
# "LF will be replaced by CRLF" warning on nearly every commit.
* text=auto

# Binary formats must never be line-ending converted — doing so corrupts them.
# *.onnx does not match visual_ai.onnx.data (its extension is .data, not
# .onnx) -- caught staging it with `text: auto` still in effect, which is
# exactly the kind of silent corruption this section exists to prevent.
*.png binary
*.webp binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.pt binary
*.onnx binary
*.onnx.data binary
*.pkl binary
*.zip binary
